## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/constant.html
- Summary (EN): The Constant node fills every pixel of a layer or VDB with a fixed value, limited to areas allowed by an optional mask. It is useful to produce a single colour or number to multiply other data by.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Constant remplit chaque pixel d'une couche ou d'un VDB avec une valeur ou une couleur fixe, limitée par un masque optionnel.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the layer or VDB to set to the constant value", "mask (optional): per-pixel amount scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by source; decides whether Value or Color applies", "Mask: how much of the new value is mixed in, default 1", "Toggle RGB, Red, Green, Blue, Alpha: channels affected", "Value: replacement number for Mono layers, or a pair of values for UV layers", "Color: replacement colour for RGB layers, or colour plus alpha for RGBA layers"]

- Caveats: ["Pixels not covered by the mask keep their original values", "Set Signature correctly, otherwise the constant does not take effect as expected"]

